.TH APT\-TRANSPORT\-CURL 8 "2026-11-17" "apt-transport-curl 0.1" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
apt\-transport\-curl \- the https method of apt on top of curl, for Maemo 5
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /usr/lib/apt/methods/https
.SH DESCRIPTION
The method
.I https
of the apt of Maemo 5 (0.7.20) uses an old libcurl with OpenSSL 0.9.8 and speaks TLS 1.0 only, which GitHub and most servers refuse
.RB ( "tlsv1 alert protocol version" ).
This package replaces the method by a shell script that runs
.BR curl (1)
8.x with TLS 1.2 and 1.3. The original method is moved aside with
.BR dpkg\-divert (8)
to
.I /usr/lib/apt/methods/https.distrib
and comes back when the package is removed.
.PP
apt starts the method itself and talks to it by the method protocol (the messages
.BR "100 Capabilities" ,
.BR "600 URI Acquire" ,
.BR "200 URI Start" ,
.BR "201 URI Done" ,
.BR "400 URI Failure" ).
There is nothing to run by hand: add a source with an
.B https://
address, and
.B apt\-get update
or the Application Manager use the method.
.PP
Certificates are always verified with the CA bundle of the curl package.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
The packages
.BR curl ,
.BR apt\-transport\-https ,
.B bash3
(for
.IR /bin/bash )
and
.B coreutils\-gnu
(the GNU
.B mktemp
and
.BR sha256sum ;
the script puts
.I /usr/bin/gnu
first in its
.BR PATH ).
The clock of the phone must be right, or the certificate check fails.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The settings are read with
.B apt\-config
at the first request:
.TP
.B Acquire::https::CaInfo
the CA bundle (a file).
.TP
.B Acquire::https::Proxy
the proxy; "DIRECT" means none.
.TP
.B Acquire::https::Timeout
seconds, for the connection and for a stalled transfer (default 60).
.TP
.B Acquire::https::Curl\-Insecure "true"
do not check certificates. Not recommended.
.PP
.B Acquire::https::Verify\-Peer
is deliberately not used: the phone ships it as "false", which would silently turn the check off.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/apt/methods/https
the method (a script).
.TP
.I /usr/lib/apt/methods/https.distrib
the original method of apt-transport-https.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/apt-transport-curl.debug
if this file exists, the whole conversation with apt is logged to
.IR /tmp/apt-transport-curl.log .
.TP
.I /tmp/apt-transport-curl.errors
what went wrong, with the time. (/tmp is a small tmpfs of 1 MB: do not leave the debug log on.)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt\-transport\-curl\-check (8),
.BR apt\-get (8),
.BR curl (1),
.BR n900 (7)
.SH AUTHOR
elPytel. Project: https://github.com/n900-resurrection/apt-transport-curl
